    {
      "id": "claim_4d817b36d5384ad2ab7eb5bf4a6f3aa9",
      "statement": "The zf-reviewer's GitHub review-posting convention (from the reviewer skill): post verdicts via `gh pr review <n> --comment --body-file <file>` — never `--approve`/`--request-changes` (the authed identity is the PR author, so GitHub rejects self-approval) and never inline `--body` (shell-mangling risk); when terminal output looks garbled or truncated, re-check `gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/pulls/<n>/reviews` before retrying, because the first call may already have posted and posted reviews cannot be deleted — duplicates are deduped with a `gh pr comment` note naming the canonical review id.",
